WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.875
I'm living here for eight
months because I'm working

00:00:03.875 --> 00:00:08.250
in a COVID-19 center to save
my family from the virus.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:12.125
I try to make a distance from my family.

00:00:12.125 --> 00:00:16.000
This is my reason to
live here in the living room.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.625
It's hard that you live in one house,

00:00:22.625 --> 00:00:25.500
but you feel as though you live in another place.

00:00:27.875 --> 00:00:32.000
Hanna Samson is a nurse
at the St. Paul's hospital in Ethiopia.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Like many
low-income countries,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Ethiopia has struggled to secure vaccines

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.875
leaving its frontline workers
in a vulnerable position.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:44.500
In December 2020, Hanna
contracted the virus

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.250
while working at a
COVID-19 treatment center.

00:00:48.125 --> 00:00:51.125
They took me in the hospital.

00:00:53.375 --> 00:00:57.500
When I arrived at the
Millennium COVID care center

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:02.625
I lost my consciousness because I'm afraid

00:01:04.125 --> 00:01:08.500
and everybody is coming
and caring of myself.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.875
And they took me in a high dependency unit.

00:01:12.875 --> 00:01:18.625
I spent for the 16 days and
they give me oxygen, they gave

00:01:18.625 --> 00:01:25.375
me unexplainable support
for me, they saved my life.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.375
For Hannah and many
other health care workers

00:01:28.375 --> 00:01:30.250
in the world's poorest countries

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:33.375
getting a vaccine, hasn't been an option.

00:01:33.375 --> 00:01:37.375
I was afraid when I was sick

00:01:37.375 --> 00:01:42.000
and when I heard our
colleagues are dying.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:46.625
It's a difficult time for me, for my family,
for my friends, colleagues.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:51.500
But a global initiative called COVAX
is trying to ensure that people

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.625
in all corners of the world
get access to vaccines.

00:01:55.125 --> 00:01:56.625
Because of COVAX

00:01:56.625 --> 00:01:58.875
Hanna was able to get vaccinated

00:01:58.875 --> 00:02:00.250
and it might be the best bet

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:02.250
for immunizing the rest of the world too.

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:16.000
As rich countries race to
inoculate their populations

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.625
poor countries have fallen behind

00:02:17.625 --> 00:02:20.750
in the biggest vaccination
campaign in history

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:23.000
and that's a problem for everyone.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.125
Wildly uneven and unfair that's

00:02:25.125 --> 00:02:27.250
how the U.N. describes the distribution

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.250
of COVID vaccines around the world.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:31.500
Very few of those doses,
a very small proportion

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.000
of them have been used in low
and middle income countries.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.250
There's five or six of these variants

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:38.625
that I would say are of concern out there.

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:41.500
The thing that we worry
about the most, that it

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:45.500
will essentially evade the
protection of the vaccine.

00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:50.125
The pandemic has weighed
heavily on developing economies,

00:02:50.125 --> 00:02:51.875
take the example of Ethiopia.

00:02:51.875 --> 00:02:53.625
It's long been seen as one

00:02:53.625 --> 00:02:56.125
of Africa's most
promising economies,

00:02:56.125 --> 00:02:58.750
but the country has
a sizeable debt.

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:00.500
At the end of 2019

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:05.125
it's total public foreign
debts stood at $27.8 billion

00:03:05.125 --> 00:03:06.625
according to The World Bank.

00:03:07.625 --> 00:03:09.250
The pandemic has put pressure

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:11.500
on the healthcare system and the economy,

00:03:12.375 --> 00:03:15.000
leading Ethiopia to ask for debt relief

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.250
under a G20 program to
help poor countries reeling

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:21.375
under the economic impact of coronavirus.

00:03:21.375 --> 00:03:24.625
For many low-income countries,
even before the pandemic

00:03:24.625 --> 00:03:28.125
were facing financial
constraints, huge debt loads

00:03:28.125 --> 00:03:31.750
and really didn't have
the financial capacity to

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:34.875
negotiate bilateral deals
with the vaccine developers

00:03:34.875 --> 00:03:39.000
like developed countries,
Europe and the U.S. were able to.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.875
I've long argued that pandemics

00:03:40.875 --> 00:03:42.875
are an evolutionary certainty.

00:03:42.875 --> 00:03:45.250
Seth Berkley is the head of Gavi,

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:46.625
the Vaccine Alliance.

00:03:46.625 --> 00:03:48.500
He's an epidemiologist

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:51.000
and you know, he's
really devoted, you know

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.750
the past year to fighting the pandemic.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.750
He conceived of this COVAX initiative

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:01.625
at Davos in January, 2020, realizing

00:04:01.625 --> 00:04:06.375
that when the pandemic really
hit and we had vaccines

00:04:06.375 --> 00:04:10.250
the real challenge would be
providing equitable access

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:13.000
to countries that couldn't
afford to buy them on their own.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.625
My job is to try to solve
these problems and put

00:04:15.625 --> 00:04:17.625
in place systems to do that.

00:04:17.625 --> 00:04:20.500
And so at this Davos
meeting, we heard about

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:23.000
this new epidemic that was going on.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.750
It was early days, we
didn't know if there were

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:26.125
people to people, transmission

00:04:26.125 --> 00:04:28.375
but I sat down with Richard Hatchett,

00:04:28.375 --> 00:04:30.250
who's the CEO of CEPI,

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:33.500
the Coalition For Epidemic
Preparedness Innovations,

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.375
and we discussed what we were doing.

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:38.000
So that really was the
beginning of the collaboration.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.625
Of course, a lot happened since then,

00:04:40.625 --> 00:04:42.875
at the end, they focused on the R&amp;D,

00:04:42.875 --> 00:04:45.000
we focused on the
procurement and delivery,

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.875
and WHO focuses on the
normative side of things.

00:04:48.875 --> 00:04:51.000
But we came together working

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.500
like we do in the Alliance
with multiple partners.

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:54.250
For the first time

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:58.000
we've seen the whole world
come together at least in name

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.625
in terms of COVAX and
wanting to move forward.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.375
More than 190 countries are participating

00:05:04.375 --> 00:05:07.875
in the COVAX facility,
the wealthy countries

00:05:07.875 --> 00:05:11.125
are participating through
paying for their doses

00:05:11.125 --> 00:05:14.500
through this purchasing
pool that COVAX has set up,

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:17.500
while COVAX provides
the low-income countries

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:19.750
with doses for free through money

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:24.125
it is raised from governments,
development agencies,

00:05:24.125 --> 00:05:27.500
as well as, private sector contributions.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:31.625
When we decided to do COVAX,
we didn't have any deals,

00:05:31.625 --> 00:05:34.125
we didn't have any money,
we had to go out and raise money.

00:05:34.125 --> 00:05:36.625
We had to begin to talk to
manufacturers and of course

00:05:36.625 --> 00:05:38.500
to make a deal with a manufacturer

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:40.375
you have to have the finance in place.

00:05:42.625 --> 00:05:45.875
COVAX is a huge international effort.

00:05:45.875 --> 00:05:47.375
The biggest international effort

00:05:47.375 --> 00:05:49.250
since the Paris Climate Accords.

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:52.166
It has required a massive
fundraising effort

00:05:52.166 --> 00:05:54.375
from governments around the world.

00:05:54.375 --> 00:05:58.000
It's a procurement challenge,
they've had to negotiate deals

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:01.875
with pharmaceutical
companies to secure doses

00:06:01.875 --> 00:06:05.625
on timing and delivery
and then at the same time,

00:06:05.625 --> 00:06:07.375
they've had to prepare countries

00:06:07.375 --> 00:06:11.375
around the world for the
rollout on the ground.

00:06:11.375 --> 00:06:15.375
And that is but a huge, you
know, logistical challenge.

00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:19.625
The arrival of this particular
vaccine has come as a great

00:06:19.625 --> 00:06:23.000
relief to heath workers
and a lot of Ghanians.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:28.375
COVAX is aiming to deliver 2 billion
doses by the end of the year.

00:06:28.375 --> 00:06:33.500
It has so far raised almost $7 billion,
it just came out

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:37.375
with a new initiative to
raise an additional $2 billion.

00:06:37.375 --> 00:06:39.125
But there's still a long way to go,

00:06:39.125 --> 00:06:42.000
they need more money and
they need more doses.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.875
Is it enough what they have achieved?

00:06:43.875 --> 00:06:46.500
Of course it's not but it's
not a question of money

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:49.250
for the time being, it's
a question of what access

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:53.375
to vaccines are
they going to be given

00:06:53.375 --> 00:06:57.250
by others so that they can take care

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:00.125
of the majority of the world's population.

00:07:00.125 --> 00:07:02.250
What is surprising is
that wealthy countries

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:06.500
haven't donated more to
COVAX given that it's really

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:10.000
in their self-interest,
if the virus continues

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:14.625
to rage in low-income
countries, that will only mean

00:07:14.625 --> 00:07:19.875
that it's likely to boomerang
back into the developed world.

00:07:19.875 --> 00:07:22.625
New mutant strains will develop

00:07:22.625 --> 00:07:26.916
and it will be incredibly hard
to stop COVID in its tracks.

00:07:28.625 --> 00:07:31.500
Right now we have a situation
where wealthy countries have

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:35.125
orded many times of the
amount of doses they need.

00:07:36.166 --> 00:07:37.875
It's really time now to turn that around

00:07:37.875 --> 00:07:41.500
and either begin to make
those doses available

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:45.000
through dose sharing or
to free up the places

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:47.125
in the manufacturing queue

00:07:47.125 --> 00:07:49.375
and that will allow doses
to go across the world

00:07:49.375 --> 00:07:50.916
and that will allow doses
to go across the world

00:07:50.916 --> 00:07:53.291
get us to a place where
we can end the acute phase

00:07:53.291 --> 00:07:55.416
of the pandemic as quickly as possible.

00:07:56.625 --> 00:07:58.000
But it's not just the wealthiest

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.750
countries complicating COVAX's efforts.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:02.125
It's been pretty challenging

00:08:02.125 --> 00:08:04.250
for COVAX to get its own supplies,

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:07.125
vaccine nationalism is
so front and center.

00:08:07.125 --> 00:08:10.375
Vaccine nationalism is a huge challenge

00:08:10.375 --> 00:08:13.125
for the COVAX initiative,
it's heavily dependent

00:08:13.125 --> 00:08:15.875
on the AstraZeneca vaccine because of its

00:08:15.875 --> 00:08:18.375
low cost and easy distribution.

00:08:18.375 --> 00:08:20.750
AstraZeneca is producing the vaccine

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:25.375
on its own, as well as through
an independent manufacturer

00:08:25.375 --> 00:08:27.625
in India called the Serum Institute.

00:08:27.625 --> 00:08:31.375
But India itself is facing
a second way of infections

00:08:31.375 --> 00:08:35.375
and has curbed large-scale
exports of the vaccine.

00:08:37.125 --> 00:08:41.250
The other challenge that
COVAX faces is its dependency

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:45.250
on the AstraZeneca vaccine,
which has seen these reports

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:48.500
of rare blood clots
associated with the shot.

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.875
And that has given rise
to a vaccine hesitancy

00:08:50.875 --> 00:08:52.375
around the world.

00:08:52.375 --> 00:08:56.625
You've seen reports of people not showing up
and doses going to waste

00:08:56.625 --> 00:08:59.416
because of concerns about the
safety of the vaccine,

00:08:59.416 --> 00:09:03.041
even though those reports are
exceedingly rare,

00:09:03.041 --> 00:09:08.041
I think it does pose a challenge for
rolling out doses worldwide.

00:09:08.541 --> 00:09:11.041
There are also major
challenges to produce the

00:09:11.041 --> 00:09:14.291
vast quantity of vaccines
needed around the world.

00:09:14.291 --> 00:09:16.791
Normally in the world, we use about three

00:09:16.791 --> 00:09:19.666
and a half billion
doses of vaccine a year.

00:09:19.666 --> 00:09:23.375
If you add flu to that, it
ends up being about 5 billion.

00:09:23.375 --> 00:09:25.916
People are talking about trying
to cover the whole world.

00:09:25.916 --> 00:09:30.041
That would be another
10 to 15 billion doses

00:09:30.041 --> 00:09:33.041
that would have to be done
in the course of this year.

00:09:33.041 --> 00:09:36.041
That would be a quadrupling
of global supply.

00:09:36.041 --> 00:09:39.250
That is very ambitious not
just for the manufacturing

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:42.416
capacity but also the raw
materials, the supplies,

00:09:42.416 --> 00:09:45.666
the staff and so this is a
real challenge for the world.

00:09:47.875 --> 00:09:50.166
Pharmaceutical companies
have been criticized

00:09:50.166 --> 00:09:51.791
for not releasing their formulas

00:09:51.791 --> 00:09:55.416
so that more manufacturers
can produce at scale.

00:09:55.416 --> 00:09:58.791
Some say COVAX should be
doing more to pressure them.

00:09:58.791 --> 00:10:01.875
Anna Marriott, the health
policy advisor for Oxfam

00:10:01.875 --> 00:10:03.916
argues that these manufacturing issues

00:10:03.916 --> 00:10:06.500
could have been mitigated by COVAX.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:09.166
You know, I think right
from the outset COVAX

00:10:09.166 --> 00:10:12.666
should have used its enormous leverage.

00:10:12.666 --> 00:10:15.666
It could have pushed those
pharmaceutical corporations

00:10:15.666 --> 00:10:18.166
to share the vaccine science and know-how.

00:10:18.166 --> 00:10:19.916
We know that there are many offers

00:10:19.916 --> 00:10:23.500
on the table from
manufacturers, from Bangladesh,

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:27.541
Pakistan to Denmark and Canada
who are coming forward now

00:10:27.541 --> 00:10:30.291
and saying we could help
make these vaccines.

00:10:30.291 --> 00:10:32.666
If the vaccine science was shared

00:10:32.666 --> 00:10:35.875
and the intellectual property rules removed.

00:10:35.875 --> 00:10:37.375
If we'd done that much earlier

00:10:37.375 --> 00:10:40.125
on those manufacturers
could be helping us now

00:10:40.125 --> 00:10:41.416
making those vaccines.

00:10:41.416 --> 00:10:43.250
It's certainly not too late,

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:44.750
we do have to act now.

00:10:44.916 --> 00:10:45.166
But COVAX argues the issue lies

00:10:45.166 --> 00:10:47.166
But COVAX argues the issue lies

00:10:47.166 --> 00:10:50.541
in teaching other manufacturers
the detailed analytics,

00:10:50.541 --> 00:10:53.125
tests, and quality assurance procedures

00:10:53.125 --> 00:10:55.375
needed to make the vaccines.

00:10:55.375 --> 00:10:57.416
The issue is not for vaccines

00:10:57.416 --> 00:10:59.125
that patents are the blocker.

00:10:59.125 --> 00:11:00.791
There may be a patent or two,

00:11:00.791 --> 00:11:04.416
but those could be gotten
around if one needed to.

00:11:04.416 --> 00:11:07.166
The real challenge is can
you get those thousands

00:11:07.166 --> 00:11:10.666
of pages of know-how and can
you have those transferred?

00:11:12.291 --> 00:11:14.625
Beyond the immediate
manufacturing problems

00:11:14.625 --> 00:11:18.916
hampering COVAX's rollout
lies an even bigger problem.

00:11:18.916 --> 00:11:21.500
The initiatives donations
will provide doses

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:24.416
that will cover only
about 30% of populations

00:11:24.416 --> 00:11:26.166
in low-income countries.

00:11:26.166 --> 00:11:29.666
That's nowhere near what's
needed to achieve herd immunity.

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:32.875
Countries like Ethiopia for instance,

00:11:32.875 --> 00:11:36.375
is entirely dependent
on the COVAX initiative.

00:11:36.375 --> 00:11:39.291
It has something like 110 million people

00:11:39.291 --> 00:11:44.125
and so far it's only
administered about 400,000 doses.

00:11:44.125 --> 00:11:46.291
So they have a long way to go before

00:11:46.291 --> 00:11:49.500
they get anywhere near what, you know

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:52.000
scientists believe is herd immunity

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:54.166
to stop the pandemic in its tracks.

00:11:56.416 --> 00:11:58.250
COVAX may not be a silver bullet

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:00.666
to the world's vaccine equity problem,

00:12:00.666 --> 00:12:04.166
but ending the pandemic will be
almost impossible without it.

00:12:04.166 --> 00:12:07.666
Well, COVAX is this solution to it,
there is no other one.

00:12:07.666 --> 00:12:14.375
Tell me which other organization has
tried to bite the bullet here?

00:12:14.375 --> 00:12:17.000
Which other organization
has been so ambitious

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:19.791
that they are promising to do everything

00:12:19.791 --> 00:12:21.791
that it takes to give a vaccine

00:12:21.791 --> 00:12:24.166
also to those who cannot afford it?

00:12:24.166 --> 00:12:27.541
There is no other one, so
they have to be supported.

00:12:27.541 --> 00:12:29.041
Of course, at the end of the day

00:12:29.041 --> 00:12:33.291
the real question now is
will the doses be available?

00:12:33.291 --> 00:12:35.291
Will the companies make the doses?

00:12:35.291 --> 00:12:38.416
Will as high-income countries
reach a certain threshold

00:12:38.416 --> 00:12:40.250
begin to say we'll release some

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:43.625
of the excess doses that we
have and make those available?

00:12:43.625 --> 00:12:46.875
And will we be able
to scale up manufacturing?

00:12:46.875 --> 00:12:49.916
If we can do that, then
we'll be in a world where

00:12:49.916 --> 00:12:53.750
the world has been
protected during a pandemic.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:57.416
If we can't do that,
we will be in a world

00:12:57.416 --> 00:12:59.916
that is very unfair
and very inequitable

00:12:59.916 --> 00:13:04.291
and that's exactly what we're
trying to stop through COVAX.

